# Development and CI tooling for Darwin's advisory quality gates (P0.2). This file
# is the SOURCE you edit; requirements-dev.txt is the generated, hash-locked
# closure (runtime + dev tools + transitive, with --generate-hashes) and is never
# hand-edited. It is what CI installs with --require-hashes.
#
# Includes the runtime requirements (via -r requirements.in) plus the dev tools.
# Each dev tool is pinned to the stable version resolved at authoring time
# (2026-06-14). All three quality gates are advisory in CI
# (.github/workflows/quality.yml); coverage is reported, not gated
# (.github/workflows/ci.yml). Current baseline finding counts are recorded in
# docs/quality-baseline.md. The blocking flip is P7.2.
#
# Regenerate on Python 3.13:
#   pip-compile --generate-hashes --output-file=requirements-dev.txt requirements-dev.in
-r requirements.in
ruff==0.15.17
mypy==2.1.0
pytest-cov==7.1.0
